  "domain": "distributed-collaboration",
  "definition": "Notion is a cloud-based productivity and knowledge-management platform that unifies note-taking, relational databases, wikis, project management boards, and document editing into a single composable workspace. Its block-based editor treats every content element \u2014 text, tables, embeds, code, and media \u2014 as a manipulable unit that can be nested, linked, and filtered, enabling teams to construct custom workflows without traditional software development. Notion serves as an all-in-one tool replacing multiple specialised SaaS products for many knowledge workers and organisations. Since 2023 Notion has integrated generative AI capabilities directly into its editing and querying workflows.",
